 "root_cause": "Staging mkdir ran before guarded job start, leaving a queued job on failure. A queued cancellation then attempted a second terminal write. Any terminal write exception skipped cleanup, while rmtree(ignore_errors=True) suppressed the existing residual diagnostic.",
 "changes": [
  "Start the durable job before creating its staging directory; map mkdir I/O errors to failed/media_staging_unavailable without dispatch",
  "Skip repeated settlement for a job already cancelled while queued",
  "Always attempt staging cleanup in a nested finally even if settlement raises, preserving the settlement exception",
  "Report actual deletion failures with the existing fixed event and owned directory only; a missing top-level directory is already clean"
 ],
